From 91a13fce7b8cc8d0c2ee9744237fa4d63cbdb2a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Siyuan Feng <sealseacat@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 23:42:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] ci: lint, type-check, coverage gate, and security
 scanning
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- ruff (E/F/W/I/B/UP, py39 target) across src/tests/examples — codebase
  brought to zero findings; config lives in pyproject.toml
- mypy on src/dbmask (3.9 target, pinned <2 while the floor is 3.9) — two
  real narrowing bugs fixed on the way (seed-store salt race could assign
  None; Optional access in pipeline/engine now properly narrowed)
- coverage job with an 80% fail-under gate (currently ~85%)
- pip-audit job (advisory), CodeQL (weekly + per-PR), dependency-review on
  PRs (fails on newly-introduced high-severity vulns), dependabot for pip
  and GitHub Actions
- concurrency group cancels superseded runs; CONTRIBUTING documents the
  local equivalents of every gate

